.Dd 2026-10-15 20:30:00
.Dt CONCURRENCY 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm concurrency
.Nd concurrency control, dari locking sampai snapshot isolation
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Ini catatan Chapter 15 dari buku Database System Concepts.
Isinya: lock-based protocols, two-phase locking, deadlock
handling, multiple granularity, timestamp-based protocols,
validation-based protocols, multiversion schemes, snapshot
isolation, insert/delete operations, index locking, weak
levels of consistency.
.Pp
Bahasa santai. Tiap protokol dijelasin kenapa dia ada dan
trade-off-nya. Karena concurrency control itu balancing act
antara correctness dan performance.
.Ss Bagian 1: Lock-Based Protocols
.Sy Lock
= mekanisme buat control concurrent access ke data item.
.Pp
.Sy Dua mode:
.Bl -tag -width "Exclusive" -offset indent
.It Sy Exclusive (X) mode
Data item bisa dibaca dan ditulis. Request pakai
.Sy lock-X .
.It Sy Shared (S) mode
Data item cuma bisa dibaca. Request pakai
.Sy lock-S .
.El
.Sy Lock request
dibuat ke concurrency-control manager. Transaction proceed
cuma setelah request granted.
.Ss Bagian 1.1: Compatibility Matrix
.Bd -literal -offset indent
         S       X
S      true    false
X      false   false
.Ed
.Sy Aturan:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Banyak transaction bisa hold shared lock di item yang sama.
.It
Kalau ada transaction hold exclusive lock, transaction lain
nggak boleh hold lock apapun.
.It
Kalau lock nggak bisa granted, requesting transaction nunggu
sampai incompatible lock released.
.El
.Ss Bagian 1.2: Contoh Locking
.Bd -literal -offset indent
T2:
  lock-S(A)
  read(A)
  unlock(A)
  lock-S(B)
  read(B)
  unlock(B)
  display(A+B)
.Ed
.Sy Kenapa ini nggak cukup?
Kalau A dan B diupdate di antara read A dan read B, sum yang
ditampilkan salah.
.Pp
.Sy Solusi:
Locking protocol. Set of rules yang diikuti semua transaction.
Restrict set of possible schedule.
.Ss Bagian 2: Two-Phase Locking (2PL)
.Sy Protocol:
.Bl -tag -width "Phase 2" -offset indent
.It Sy Phase 1: Growing Phase
Transaction may obtain locks. May not release locks.
.It Sy Phase 2: Shrinking Phase
Transaction may release locks. May not obtain locks.
.El
.Sy Jaminan:
Conflict-serializable schedules.
.Sy Lock point:
Titik di mana transaction acquired final lock. Transaction
dapat di-serialize di order lock point.
.Ss Bagian 2.1: 2PL dengan Lock Conversions
.Bl -tag -width "Phase 2" -offset indent
.It Sy Phase 1
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Acquire lock-S on item.
.It
Acquire lock-X on item.
.It
Convert lock-S ke lock-X (upgrade).
.El
.It Sy Phase 2
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Release lock-S.
.It
Release lock-X.
.It
Convert lock-X ke lock-S (downgrade).
.El
.El
.Sy Tetap butuh programmer
buat insert locking instruction.
.Ss Bagian 2.2: Automatic Locking
.Sy read(D) diproses:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
if T_i has lock on D
    read(D)
else
    if necessary wait until no other transaction has lock-X on D
    grant T_i lock-S on D
    read(D)
.Ed
.Sy write(D) diproses:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
if T_i has lock-X on D
    write(D)
else
    if necessary wait until no other transaction has any lock on D
    if T_i has lock-S on D
        upgrade lock on D ke lock-X
    else
        grant T_i lock-X on D
    write(D)
.Ed
.Sy All locks released after commit or abort.
.Ss Bagian 3: Deadlock
.Sy Contoh:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
T3                T4
lock-X(B)
read(B)
B := B - 50
write(B)
lock-X(A)
                  lock-S(A)
                  read(A)
                  lock-S(B)
.Ed
.Sy Masalah:
T3 nunggu T4 release lock A, T4 nunggu T3 release lock B.
.Sy Deadlock.
.Pp
.Sy Solusi:
Roll back salah satu transaction, release locks.
.Ss Bagian 3.1: Deadlock vs Starvation
.Sy 2PL nggak ensure freedom from deadlock.
.Pp
.Sy Starvation:
Terjadi kalau concurrency control manager badly designed.
Contoh: transaction nunggu X-lock, sementara sequence of
transaction request dan granted S-lock. Transaction yang sama
repeatedly rolled back.
.Ss Bagian 3.2: Strict dan Rigorous 2PL
.Bl -tag -width "Rigorous" -offset indent
.It Sy Strict 2PL
Transaction must hold all its exclusive locks till it
commits/aborts. Avoid cascading rollback.
.It Sy Rigorous 2PL
All locks held till commit/abort. Transaction dapat
di-serialize di order commit.
.El
.Ss Bagian 4: Implementation of Locking
.Sy Lock manager:
Separate process yang terima lock/unlock request.
.Pp
.Sy Lock table:
In-memory hash table indexed on data item name.
.Pp
.Sy Queue:
New request added ke end of queue. Granted kalau compatible
dengan semua earlier locks.
.Ss Bagian 5: Deadlock Handling
.Ss Bagian 5.1: Deadlock Prevention
.Bl -tag -width "Timeout" -offset indent
.It Sy Predeclaration
Lock semua data item sebelum mulai execution.
.It Sy Partial ordering
Impose partial ordering ke data item. Lock hanya in order.
.It Sy Wait-die (non-preemptive)
Older transaction may wait for younger. Younger nggak nunggu
older, mereka rolled back.
.It Sy Wound-wait (preemptive)
Older transaction wounds (force rollback) younger.
Younger may wait for older.
.It Sy Timeout-based
Transaction nunggu lock hanya specified time. Kalau nggak
dapet, rollback dan restart.
.El
.Ss Bagian 5.2: Deadlock Detection
.Sy Wait-for graph:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
V = set of vertices (all transaction).
.It
E = set of edges; ordered pair T_i -> T_j.
.It
Kalau T_i -> T_j in E, T_i waiting for T_j to release data item.
.El
.Sy System deadlocked
jika dan hanya jika wait-for graph punya cycle.
.Pp
.Sy Recovery:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Pilih victim transaction yang incur minimum cost.
.It
Total rollback atau partial rollback.
.It
Include number of rollbacks in cost factor buat avoid starvation.
.El
.Ss Bagian 6: Multiple Granularity
.Sy Data item
bisa various sizes. Define hierarchy of data granularities.
.Pp
.Sy Contoh hierarki:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
          DB
         /  \
        A1   A2
       /  \    \
     Fa    Fb   Fc
    / | \  /|\  /|\
   r  r  r r r r r r
.Ed
.Sy Levels:
database, area, file, record.
.Pp
.Sy Locking granularity:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Fine granularity (lower): high concurrency, high overhead.
.It
Coarse granularity (higher): low overhead, low concurrency.
.El
.Ss Bagian 6.1: Intention Lock Modes
.Bl -tag -width "SIX" -offset indent
.It Sy IS (Intention-Shared)
Indicates explicit locking at lower level with shared locks.
.It Sy IX (Intention-Exclusive)
Indicates explicit locking at lower level with exclusive or
shared locks.
.It Sy SIX (Shared + Intention-Exclusive)
Subtree locked explicitly in shared mode, plus explicit
locking at lower level with exclusive-mode locks.
.El
.Sy Kenapa intention lock?
Biar higher level node bisa di-lock S atau X tanpa harus
check semua descendent nodes.
.Ss Bagian 7: Timestamp-Based Protocols
.Sy Setiap transaction
dikasih timestamp saat enter system.
.Sy TS(T_i) < TS(T_j)
berarti T_i older.
.Pp
.Sy Protocol maintain untuk tiap data Q:
.Bl -tag -width "W-timestamp" -offset indent
.It Sy W-timestamp(Q)
Largest timestamp of any transaction yang sukses write(Q).
.It Sy R-timestamp(Q)
Largest timestamp of any transaction yang sukses read(Q).
.El
.Ss Bagian 7.1: Timestamp Ordering Protocol
.Sy Read(Q):
.Bl -enun -offset indent
.It
Kalau TS(T_i) <= W-timestamp(Q), T_i perlu baca value yang udah
overwritten. Reject, rollback T_i.
.It
Kalau TS(T_i) >= W-timestamp(Q), execute read, set
R-timestamp(Q) = max(R-timestamp(Q), TS(T_i)).
.El
.Sy Write(Q):
.Bl -enun -offset indent
.It
Kalau TS(T_i) < R-timestamp(Q), value yang diproduksi udah
dibutuhin sebelumnya. Reject, rollback T_i.
.It
Kalau TS(T_i) < W-timestamp(Q), attempt to write obsolete
value. Reject, rollback T_i.
.It
Otherwise, execute write, set W-timestamp(Q) = TS(T_i).
.El
.Ss Bagian 7.2: Thomas' Write Rule
.Sy Modified version:
Obsolete write operations bisa di-ignore.
.Pp
.Sy Kalau TS(T_i) < W-timestamp(Q):
Daripada rollback, write di-ignore.
.Pp
.Sy Allows view-serializable schedules
yang bukan conflict-serializable. Greater concurrency.
.Ss Bagian 8: Validation-Based Protocols
.Sy Juga disebut optimistic concurrency control.
.Pp
.Sy Tiga fase:
.Bl -enun -offset indent
.It
.Sy Read and execution phase:
Transaction writes only to temporary local variables.
.It
.Sy Validation phase:
Transaction perform "validation test" buat determine kalau
local variables bisa ditulis tanpa violate serializability.
.It
.Sy Write phase:
Kalau validated, updates applied ke database. Kalau nggak,
rollback.
.El
.Ss Bagian 8.1: Validation Test
.Sy Setiap transaction T_i punya 3 timestamp:
.Bl -tag -width "Finish" -offset indent
.It Sy Start(T_i)
Time when T_i started execution.
.It Sy Validation(T_i)
Time when T_i entered validation phase.
.It Sy Finish(T_i)
Time when T_i finished write phase.
.El
.Sy Validation succeeds kalau untuk semua T_j dengan
TS(T_j) < TS(T_i), either:
.Bl -enun -offset indent
.It
.Sy finish(T_j) < start(T_i) :
Nggak ada overlap execution.
.It
.Sy start(T_j) < finish(T_j) < validation(T_i)
dan set data item yang ditulis T_j nggak intersect dengan set
data item yang dibaca T_i.
.El
.Ss Bagian 9: Multiversion Schemes
.Sy Ide:
Keep old versions of data item buat increase concurrency.
.Pp
.Sy Setiap write
creates new version.
.Sy Timestamps
label versions.
.Sy Read(Q):
Select appropriate version based on timestamp. Reads never
wait.
.Ss Bagian 9.1: Multiversion Timestamp Ordering
.Sy Tiap data item Q punya sequence of versions:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
<Q_1, Q_2, ..., Q_m>
.Ed
.Sy Tiap version Q_k contains:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Content (value).
.It
W-timestamp(Q_k) = timestamp of transaction yang create.
.It
R-timestamp(Q_k) = largest timestamp yang read version ini.
.El
.Sy Read(Q):
Return content of version Q_k.
.Sy Write(Q):
.Bl -enun -offset indent
.It
Kalau TS(T_i) < R-timestamp(Q_k), rollback T_i.
.It
Kalau TS(T_i) = W-timestamp(Q_k), overwrite content.
.It
Else, create new version.
.El
.Ss Bagian 9.2: Multiversion 2PL
.Sy Bedain read-only dan update transaction.
.Pp
.Sy Update transaction:
Acquire read dan write locks, hold sampai end. Follow
rigorous 2PL.
.Pp
.Sy Read-only transaction:
Assigned timestamp dengan baca current ts-counter sebelum
execution.
.Ss Bagian 10: Snapshot Isolation
.Sy Motivasi:
Decision support queries yang baca banyak data conflict
dengan OLTP transaction yang update beberapa row.
.Pp
.Sy Solusi:
Give logical "snapshot" of database state ke read-only
transaction.
.Ss Bagian 10.1: Snapshot Isolation (SI)
.Sy Transaction T1 executing dengan SI:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Takes snapshot of committed data at start.
.It
Always reads/modifies data in its own snapshot.
.It
Updates of concurrent transactions nggak visible.
.It
Writes of T1 complete when commit.
.It
First-committer-wins: commit hanya kalau nggak ada concurrent
transaction yang udah write data yang T1 mau write.
.El
.Ss Bagian 10.2: Snapshot Read
.Sy Concurrent updates invisible to snapshot read.
.Pp
.Sy Contoh:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
X_0 = 100, Y_0 = 0

T1 deposits 50 in Y      T2 withdraws 50 from X
r1(X0, 100)
                         r2(Y0, 0)
                         r2(X0, 100)
                         w2(X2, 50)
r1(Y0, 0)
w1(Y1, 50)
r1(X0, 100) (update by T2 not seen)
r1(Y1, 50) (can see own updates)
                         r2(Y0, 0) (update by T1 not seen)

X_2 = 50, Y_1 = 50
.Ed
.Ss Bagian 10.3: First-Committer-Wins
.Bd -literal -offset indent
T1                        T2
W(Y := 1)
Commit
                          Start
                          R(X) -> 0
                          R(Y) -> 1
                          W(X:=2)
                          W(Z:=3)
                          Commit
R(Z) -> 0
R(Y) -> 1
W(X:=3)
Commit-Req
Abort
.Ed
.Ss Bagian 10.4: Write Skew
.Sy Masalah SI:
SI nggak selalu give serializable execution.
.Pp
.Sy Contoh:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
T1: x:=y
T2: y:=x
Initially x = 3 dan y = 17
.Ed
.Sy Serial execution:
Either x=3, y=3 atau x=17, y=17.
.Sy Snapshot isolation:
Both start at same time, neither sees other's write.
Result: x=17, y=3 (atau sebaliknya). Inconsistent.
.Ss Bagian 10.5: SI di Praktek
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Oracle dan PostgreSQL <9.1 support SI.
.It
PostgreSQL 9.1 introduced "Serializable Snapshot Isolation" (SSI)
yang guarantee true serializability.
.It
Can sidestep SI dengan
.Sy select ... for update .
.El
.Ss Bagian 11: Insert dan Delete Operations
.Sy Kalau pakai 2PL:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Delete operation only if transaction punya exclusive lock on
tuple to be deleted.
.It
Insert operation: transaction dikasih X-mode lock on tuple.
.El
.Ss Bagian 11.1: Phantom Phenomenon
.Sy Masalah:
Transaction scan relation (e.g., find sum of balances), dan
transaction lain insert tuple. Conflict despite not accessing
tuple in common.
.Pp
.Sy Contoh:
Scan transaction nggak lihat account baru, tapi reads some
other tuple yang ditulis update transaction.
.Ss Bagian 11.2: Index Locking Protocol
.Sy Aturan:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Setiap relation harus punya minimal satu index.
.It
Transaction access tuple hanya setelah finding lewat index.
.It
Transaction yang perform lookup must lock all index leaf
nodes yang accessed, in S-mode.
.It
Transaction yang insert/update/delete must obtain exclusive
locks on all index leaf nodes affected.
.El
.Ss Bagian 12: Weak Levels of Consistency
.Bl -tag -width "Cursor stability" -offset indent
.It Sy Degree-two consistency
S-locks may be released at any time, locks may be acquired at
any time. X-locks held till end.
.It Sy Cursor stability
For reads, each tuple locked, read, lock immediately released.
X-locks held till end.
.El
.Ss Bagian 12.1: SQL Isolation Levels
.Bl -tag -width "Read uncommitted" -offset indent
.It Sy Serializable
Default.
.It Sy Repeatable read
Only committed records, repeated reads same value. Phantom
phenomenon nggak prevented.
.It Sy Read committed
Same as degree two consistency, tapi kebanyakan sistem
implement as cursor stability.
.It Sy Read uncommitted
Bahkan uncommitted data bisa dibaca.
.El
.Ss Bagian 13: Transactions Across User Interaction
.Sy Masalah:
Banyak aplikasi butuh transaction support across user
interaction. Nggak bisa pakai locking. Nggak mau reserve
database connection per user.
.Pp
.Sy Solusi:
Application level concurrency control.
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Each tuple punya version number.
.It
Transaction notes version number when reading tuple.
.It
When writing tuple, check current version number sama dengan
version when tuple was read.
.El
.Sy Equivalent:
Optimistic concurrency control without validating read set.
.Sy Used:
Hibernate ORM, dan manually in many applications.
.Ss Ringkasan
.Bd -literal -offset indent
Konsep                Inti
Lock                  Mekanisme control access
Exclusive lock        Read + write
Shared lock           Read only
Compatibility matrix  S vs S compatible, else no
2PL                   Growing phase, shrinking phase
Lock point            Titik di mana acquire final lock
Strict 2PL            Hold X-locks till commit
Rigorous 2PL          Hold all locks till commit
Deadlock              Mutual wait
Wait-die              Older waits younger
Wound-wait            Older wounds younger
Timeout               Wait for specified time
Wait-for graph        Detect deadlock via cycle
Granularity           Hierarchy of data items
Intention lock        Lock higher level without check descendent
Timestamp ordering    Order by transaction timestamp
Thomas' Write Rule    Ignore obsolete write
Validation            Optimistic, validate before write
Multiversion          Keep old versions
Snapshot isolation    Each transaction sees snapshot
First-committer-wins  Commit hanya kalau no conflict
Write skew            Anomaly SI
Phantom phenomenon    Insert conflict with scan
Index locking         Prevent phantom
Degree-two            S-locks released anytime
Cursor stability      Tuple locked read release
SQL isolation level   Serializable, repeatable read,
                      read committed, read uncommitted
.Ed
Kalau kamu cuma inget satu hal dari catatan ini, inget ini:
.Sy concurrency control itu trade-off antara correctness dan
performance. 2PL guarantee serializability tapi bisa deadlock.
Timestamp ordering nggak deadlock tapi bisa cascading
rollback. Snapshot isolation performa bagus tapi bisa write
skew. Nggak ada satu protokol yang perfect buat semua kasus.
.Pp
Yang belum dijawab di sini: gimana caranya recovery setelah
crash? Gimana caranya implement distributed transaction?
Itu topik lanjutan: recovery system, distributed database.
